{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836236",
      "title": "Module Introduction & Starting Project",
      "sourceHash": "64808188c66fd920732cdb6e300fa6e257ec911813239761bb1b599ec090ed1e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.84,
          "end": 2.52,
          "en": "This course section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.52,
          "end": 4.95,
          "en": "is about Refs and Portals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.95,
          "end": 9.03,
          "en": "Two slightly more advanced React concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.03,
          "end": 10.669,
          "en": "which you definitely don't need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.669,
          "end": 14.04,
          "en": "in all React apps you are going to build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.04,
          "end": 16.98,
          "en": "After all, we did not need those features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.98,
          "end": 19.8,
          "en": "in the demo apps we built up to this point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.8,
          "end": 24.254,
          "en": "But two features which can simplify certain things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.254,
          "end": 28.44,
          "en": "and also help you solve certain problems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.44,
          "end": 33.18,
          "en": "which otherwise are almost impossible to solve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.18,
          "end": 36.06,
          "en": "And therefore, in this course section here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.06,
          "end": 39.69,
          "en": "you will learn what Refs are and how you can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.69,
          "end": 44.69,
          "en": "use this Refs feature to gain simplified direct access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45,
          "end": 49.83,
          "en": "to DOM Elements and what you can do with that access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.83,
          "end": 54.03,
          "en": "You will also learn how you can also use this Refs feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 58.41,
          "en": "to manage values that shouldn't be State.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.41,
          "end": 62.49,
          "en": "And you'll see when exactly that could be the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.49,
          "end": 65.328,
          "en": "And you will also learn how you can build Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.328,
          "end": 68.22,
          "en": "that expose an API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.22,
          "end": 72.57,
          "en": "For example, callable functions to other Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.57,
          "end": 75.78,
          "en": "with help of that Refs concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.78,
          "end": 80.22,
          "en": "And then, this section of course also is about Portals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 80.22,
          "end": 82.53,
          "en": "and you will learn what Portals are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.53,
          "end": 85.35,
          "en": "and how you can use this Portals feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.35,
          "end": 88.95,
          "en": "to detach the place where an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.95,
          "end": 91.23,
          "en": "gets rendered in the actual DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.23,
          "end": 94.893,
          "en": "from the place where you use it in your JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.85,
          "end": 98.19,
          "en": "And obviously at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.19,
          "end": 100.968,
          "en": "this definitely all sounds pretty abstract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.968,
          "end": 104.25,
          "en": "and is probably all pretty confusing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.25,
          "end": 106.5,
          "en": "But that's why we're now going to dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.5,
          "end": 109.8,
          "en": "into a new demo project, which will allow us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.8,
          "end": 111.6,
          "en": "to use all these features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.6,
          "end": 113.4,
          "en": "And step by step along the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.4,
          "end": 116.34,
          "en": "you will therefore then learn how to use them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.34,
          "end": 121.32,
          "en": "Now, in this section we are going to build this demo project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.32,
          "end": 125.37,
          "en": "which in the end is kind of a game where website visitors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.37,
          "end": 128.55,
          "en": "can start different timer challenges",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.55,
          "end": 131.73,
          "en": "with the goal of estimating when time is up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.73,
          "end": 135.24,
          "en": "and stopping the timer early enough before it expires.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.24,
          "end": 139.65,
          "en": "And we're going to build that game with Refs and Portals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.65,
          "end": 141.93,
          "en": "and of course, also Components and State,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.93,
          "end": 144.9,
          "en": "and all these things about which you already learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 148.68,
          "en": "And as always, you'll find a starting project attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.68,
          "end": 150.51,
          "en": "Both a local project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.51,
          "end": 153.99,
          "en": "and a CodeSandbox project link, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.99,
          "end": 155.406,
          "en": "And in that starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.406,
          "end": 159.6,
          "en": "you'll find a pretty basic app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 162.96,
          "en": "and one custom component, a player component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.96,
          "end": 165.03300000000002,
          "en": "which also is pretty basic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.93,
          "end": 169.41,
          "en": "And if you start that development server locally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.41,
          "end": 171.72,
          "en": "after installing the dependencies locally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.72,
          "end": 172.97,
          "en": "as you always need to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.24,
          "end": 177.45,
          "en": "you don't need to do that on CodeSandbox, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.45,
          "end": 180.81,
          "en": "After doing that, if you visit the website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.81,
          "end": 183.84,
          "en": "you should see something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.84,
          "end": 185.91,
          "en": "And please note that at the moment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.91,
          "end": 188.25,
          "en": "this input here won't really work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.25,
          "end": 190.89,
          "en": "If you click Set Name, nothing happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.89,
          "end": 194.07,
          "en": "But that will now be the first thing on which will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.07,
          "end": 197.073,
          "en": "And that will be the first example for using Refs.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}